      "evidence": "Hardening note, not a real defect: this is a loopback-only, single-hop dev proxy with no cache or downstream intermediary to desync, and a client able to set `Connection: x-foo` could send `x-foo` directly anyway. The same fixed-set omission pre-exists in the response direction (proxy.ts:30-36). Everything else checked out: root cause confirmed by reproduction (pre-fix socket lingers with 0 error listeners and backend reset yields uncaughtException ECONNRESET; post-fix Node sends `connection: close` and the socket is destroyed, including for chunked POSTs and even against a non-compliant backend that answers `keep-alive` to a `close` request). Stripping breaks nothing: `expect`/`te` untouched, `transfer-encoding` deliberately retained, handleUpgrade (431-563) and handleExtendedConnect (573-719) unchanged, HTTP/1.1 upgrades never reach handleRequest (upgrade listeners at 828/786/752), all 9 WebSocket tests pass. Tests verified to fail pre-fix: `expected 'keep-alive' to be 'close'` (proxy.test.ts:189) and captured ECONNRESET (proxy.test.ts:223); chunked-DELETE guard (proxy.test.ts:264) passes both ways by design."
